# verify/ harness local overrides (git-ignored; do NOT commit .env).
#
# The CI workflow sets these explicitly, so this file exists only for local
# runs of verify/run-verify.sh on the runner from a checked-out tree.
#
# Models are defined in verify/models.json - each entry names a served model,
# its pinned snapshot revision, its own serve flags + tuning, and a `tests` map
# that selects which optional suites (tool, reasoning, multimodal, spec-decode)
# to run for that model. The driver loops the catalog (or a subset) and tests
# each model consecutively.
#
# Most served models are public; gemma-4-12B is gated on HuggingFace, so it
# needs a read token. If you serve any gated model, set a read token here.

# The vllm-gb10 image to serve (defaults to the canonical latest locally).
# IMAGE=ghcr.io/timothystewart6/vllm-gb10:v0.30.0-gb10.2

# Host port the vLLM server binds (isolated on the runner).
# VLLM_PORT=8010

# Which catalog models to run (comma-separated names from verify/models.json).
# Omit to run every model in the catalog. Legacy single-model: MODEL=<name>.
# MODELS=nemotron-lightning

# Host dirs (NFS defaults the runner already reads).
# HF_CACHE=/mnt/llm/models/huggingface
# VLLM_CACHE=/mnt/llm/vllm-compile-cache

# Host dir bind-mounted at /results in the container for result JSON.
# VERIFY_RESULT_DIR=./results

# llama-benchy prompt/generation lengths (word-split lists).
# BENCH_RUNS=3
# BENCH_PP="128 2048 8192 32768"
# BENCH_TG="32 128"
# Pinned llama-benchy release invoked via uvx (a reviewed build input).
# BENCHY_VERSION=0.4.0

# llama-benchy concurrency workload (separate fixed shape across levels).
# BENCH_CONC_PP=2048
# BENCH_CONC_TG=128
# BENCH_CONC="1 4"

# Deterministic functional-test token.
# DETERMINISTIC_TOKEN=GB10_TEST_OK

# Serve the vLLM container unprivileged (default false). The harness runs
# unprivileged unless a model needs a capability an unprivileged container
# cannot supply; re-review the security posture before enabling.
# VLLM_PRIVILEGED=false
